# The review ledger is APPEND-ONLY, so the only correct resolution of a conflict in
# it is "keep both sides' rows" — which is exactly what git's built-in `union` merge
# driver does. Every branch that changes the published tree appends here, so without
# this line every parallel branch collides on this one file and each one is resolved
# by hand; that hand-resolution is also the one place a row could be dropped, which
# an append-only record cannot survive.
#
# This is safe ONLY because every row records its own `base:`. Concatenating two
# branches' rows re-orders them, and a row whose range start is DERIVED from its
# position in the list would silently be re-parented onto the other branch's last
# commit — a range that never existed. A row that names its own base cannot be.
# See "A ROW'S OWN BASE" in automation/publish/review_gate.py before removing this.
#
# `union` is a built-in driver: no `git config merge.*` is needed for it to work.
automation/publish/review_ledger.yaml merge=union
